            "Cubic system. Small rounded dodecahedra or octahedra, mostly as grains a few millimetres across. Distinct dodecahedral cleavage; conchoidal to uneven fracture. Hardness 5.5 to 6; specific gravity 2.44 to 2.50; vitreous to greasy lustre; refractive index 1.496 to 1.510; isotropic. Orange-red fluorescence under long-wave UV in some stones. Faceted stones very rarely exceed 1 carat: a clean 0.5-carat haüyne is already exceptional. Fragile and cleavable, it is a collector's gem, best set in a pendant or earrings rather than a ring.",
